    <body>
      <div type="clause" n="3.2">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:Swer">Swer</ref> 3.2</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="3.2" corresp="#wit-b">7 swa ic hit tyme, swa hit me se sealde, ðe ic hit nu on hand sette.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="3.2" corresp="#wit-q">Et sic aduoco, sicut hoc mihi uendidit, cui nunc in manu mitto.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="3.2" corresp="#wit-h">7 swa ic hit tyme, swa hit me se sealde, ðe ic hit nu on hand sette.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#unattributed" corresp="#wit-h">[Alternatively:] And so I give a [written] guarantee that they [the cattle] were sold to me by the person in whose hands I now place it.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="de" source="#liebermann">Beziehungsweise: só schieb ich es zur Gewähr, wie es mir dér veräussert hat, dem ich es jetzt in die Hand lege.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude" ana="#fromGerman">Or: I vouch it to warranty just as he sold it to me into whose hand I now place it.</ab>
        <note type="comparedBy" source="#liebermann"><ref target="clause:Becwaeth_2">Becwæð 2</ref></note>
        <note type="editorial">Liebermann compares Duns 8.2.</note>
      </div>
    </body>
